WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:03.823
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:00:11.820 --> 00:00:15.390
CORBETT: Welcome, on behalf
of the Program in Writing

00:00:15.390 --> 00:00:19.590
and Humanistic Studies and
the Center for Bilingual

00:00:19.590 --> 00:00:20.955
and Bicultural Studies.

00:00:25.080 --> 00:00:28.050
When I see a photograph of
Jhumpa Lahiri in the New York

00:00:28.050 --> 00:00:34.710
Times or The New Yorker, I don't
think hot young fiction writer,

00:00:34.710 --> 00:00:39.000
but instead, friend
of my daughter Marni.

00:00:39.000 --> 00:00:42.960
And I remember the year or
so that Jhumpa and Marni

00:00:42.960 --> 00:00:46.650
worked at WordsWorth
bookstore in Cambridge.

00:00:46.650 --> 00:00:48.990
They tore up the place.

00:00:48.990 --> 00:00:53.640
I liked to go in and browse
just to hear them laugh.

00:00:53.640 --> 00:00:56.760
They were at that stage of
discovering their friendship

00:00:56.760 --> 00:00:59.260
when everything is hilarious.

00:00:59.260 --> 00:01:03.090
I can still hear them
bawl out-- oh, my god!

00:01:03.090 --> 00:01:05.570
[LAUGHTER]

00:01:05.570 --> 00:01:11.220
At some juicy bit of gossip
or off-the-charts exploit.

00:01:11.220 --> 00:01:14.010
Some time after
this, Jhumpa asked

00:01:14.010 --> 00:01:17.040
me to read one of
her early stories.

00:01:17.040 --> 00:01:23.010
I did so, felt lukewarm
about it, and told her so.

00:01:23.010 --> 00:01:25.695
She never showed me
another one of her stories.

00:01:25.695 --> 00:01:29.210
[LAUGHTER]

00:01:29.210 --> 00:01:31.490
I respect her for this.

00:01:31.490 --> 00:01:34.250
Writers ought to be
ruthless about their art.

00:01:34.250 --> 00:01:38.390
And they need to know where to
go to get what they require.

00:01:38.390 --> 00:01:41.000
Jhumpa began to find
what she needed while

00:01:41.000 --> 00:01:45.380
in the BU writing program,
and more and more in herself.

00:01:45.380 --> 00:01:48.830
As one thing led to another,
and with the publication

00:01:48.830 --> 00:01:52.640
of Interpreter of Maladies,
she became a star.

00:01:52.640 --> 00:01:58.400
She began as a paperback writer
and graduated to hardcover.

00:01:58.400 --> 00:02:00.590
Who knows how this happened?

00:02:00.590 --> 00:02:03.050
Bad things happen
to good writers.

00:02:03.050 --> 00:02:05.720
And when good things
happen to deserving ones,

00:02:05.720 --> 00:02:09.259
it's not easy to figure out why.

00:02:09.259 --> 00:02:11.660
A possible explanation
occurred to me

00:02:11.660 --> 00:02:13.700
when I began to
see Jhumpa grouped

00:02:13.700 --> 00:02:16.370
with Indian and Asian writers.

00:02:16.370 --> 00:02:21.110
Her work tells, at least on one
level, the old American tale

00:02:21.110 --> 00:02:25.280
of here and there, the old
country and the new world,

00:02:25.280 --> 00:02:28.370
the tale that has been ours
since the Great Immigration

00:02:28.370 --> 00:02:31.430
at the end of the 19th and
beginning of the 20th century,

00:02:31.430 --> 00:02:34.550
the tale told by Saul
Bellow and James Baldwin,

00:02:34.550 --> 00:02:39.830
by Jamaica Kincaid, and writers
will leap into all your minds.

00:02:39.830 --> 00:02:44.090
It is the American story of
who we are, how we know it,

00:02:44.090 --> 00:02:48.440
and the anxieties and
exhilarations involved.

00:02:48.440 --> 00:02:52.190
Not that this answers the
question, which in the end

00:02:52.190 --> 00:02:53.930
does not matter.

00:02:53.930 --> 00:02:58.000
Jhumpa's work has struck a
nerve, or you wouldn't be here.

00:02:58.000 --> 00:03:00.608
Jhumpa, the audience is yours.

00:03:00.608 --> 00:03:04.094
[APPLAUSE]

00:03:22.520 --> 00:03:23.516
LAHIRI: Wow.

00:03:23.516 --> 00:03:26.520
[LAUGHTER]

00:03:26.520 --> 00:03:28.420
Good evening.

00:03:28.420 --> 00:03:30.760
I am very pleased to be here.

00:03:30.760 --> 00:03:32.415
Thank you all for coming.

00:03:37.890 --> 00:03:42.970
I want to thank everyone at
MIT for having me here tonight.

00:03:42.970 --> 00:03:45.960
MIT was, as some
of you may know,

00:03:45.960 --> 00:03:50.460
the first place my father
worked in this country, when

00:03:50.460 --> 00:03:54.570
he moved here with me
and my mother in 1969.

00:03:54.570 --> 00:03:58.050
And I'm honored that it's the
first university in Boston

00:03:58.050 --> 00:04:01.740
that's asked me to read.

00:04:01.740 --> 00:04:09.210
I especially want to thank Bill
and his wife, Beverly Corbett--

00:04:09.210 --> 00:04:13.920
I want to thank Bill for his
very kind words just now--

00:04:13.920 --> 00:04:16.920
but for their efforts
and their generosity

00:04:16.920 --> 00:04:18.760
and their incredible
hospitality,

00:04:18.760 --> 00:04:22.320
which I've been a recipient
of for a long time now.

00:04:22.320 --> 00:04:28.290
I first met them 11 years ago,
right around this time of year.

00:04:28.290 --> 00:04:30.480
As Bill mentioned, I was--

00:04:30.480 --> 00:04:33.210
I am a friend of their
daughter Marni's.

00:04:33.210 --> 00:04:36.120
And at the time, I had
just moved to Boston.

00:04:36.120 --> 00:04:38.010
I'd just graduated from college.

00:04:38.010 --> 00:04:40.010
And I moved to Cambridge.

00:04:40.010 --> 00:04:44.340
And I was living in
a room of the home

00:04:44.340 --> 00:04:49.800
of a woman with these two,
shall we say, very strident

00:04:49.800 --> 00:04:50.990
young children.

00:04:50.990 --> 00:04:54.030
And I sort of lived in this
little room behind their living

00:04:54.030 --> 00:04:57.430
room, and felt very--

00:04:57.430 --> 00:04:58.510
very not at home.

00:04:58.510 --> 00:05:00.984
There were all sorts of
rules I had to abide by.

00:05:00.984 --> 00:05:02.900
I couldn't have visitors
after a certain hour.

00:05:02.900 --> 00:05:04.830
I had to wipe down
the stove every time

00:05:04.830 --> 00:05:06.840
I boiled water for tea--

00:05:06.840 --> 00:05:08.470
all of these things.

00:05:08.470 --> 00:05:11.910
Was not a very ideal situation.

00:05:11.910 --> 00:05:15.210
And it was around that time
that Marni invited me to dinner

00:05:15.210 --> 00:05:16.770
at her parents' house.

00:05:16.770 --> 00:05:18.990
I remember it was
a Sunday night.

00:05:18.990 --> 00:05:21.900
And I had directions
to go to the South End.

00:05:21.900 --> 00:05:24.060
I'd never been to
the South End before.

00:05:24.060 --> 00:05:26.680
I got on the Orange Line
and went the wrong way;

00:05:26.680 --> 00:05:30.030
found myself heading
rapidly toward Oak Grove.

00:05:30.030 --> 00:05:34.380
Turned back around and made
it, eventually, to their house.

00:05:34.380 --> 00:05:38.700
And was immediately
just so struck.

00:05:38.700 --> 00:05:41.805
Those first weeks of my
life in Boston were very--

00:05:44.420 --> 00:05:45.600
they weren't too pleasant.

00:05:45.600 --> 00:05:49.830
And all of a sudden, I
felt wonderfully at home.

00:05:49.830 --> 00:05:54.690
And I discovered a beautiful
home and beautiful people

00:05:54.690 --> 00:05:58.871
and good food, and rules
that were decidedly relaxed--

00:05:58.871 --> 00:05:59.370
[LAUGHTER]

00:05:59.370 --> 00:06:02.580
Compared to my own lodgings.

00:06:02.580 --> 00:06:07.440
And that was the first of many
nights I spent in their home,

00:06:07.440 --> 00:06:11.010
and many delicious dinners
I ate at their table--

00:06:11.010 --> 00:06:14.217
another of which I'm about
to have in a few hours.

00:06:14.217 --> 00:06:15.300
I'm looking forward to it.

00:06:15.300 --> 00:06:18.410
[LAUGHTER]

00:06:18.410 --> 00:06:21.400
And I also want to say that
it was also around this time

00:06:21.400 --> 00:06:25.660
that I went to my first
reading in Boston.

00:06:25.660 --> 00:06:27.920
And that was one
of Bill's readings.

00:06:27.920 --> 00:06:32.050
He was reading from his book
On Blue Note up at Harvard.

00:06:32.050 --> 00:06:34.780
And I remember going
with Marni and Beverly,

00:06:34.780 --> 00:06:38.770
and feeling very
excited about this.

00:06:38.770 --> 00:06:44.650
Until I met Bill, I hadn't
known a writer before.

00:06:44.650 --> 00:06:49.030
Writers were, to me, names
on the covers of books.

00:06:49.030 --> 00:06:52.000
But they weren't people.

00:06:52.000 --> 00:06:56.200
And I was amazed,
over the months

00:06:56.200 --> 00:06:58.690
that I grew to know their
family, that here was

00:06:58.690 --> 00:07:02.830
this man who had a
family and a house,

00:07:02.830 --> 00:07:05.260
and wrote all these
books, and had a life,

00:07:05.260 --> 00:07:08.890
and even managed to throw all
these amazing dinner parties.

00:07:08.890 --> 00:07:12.730
And so I want to thank him
for that wonderful example.

00:07:12.730 --> 00:07:16.000
And I think that if I could
write half as many books

00:07:16.000 --> 00:07:18.460
and throw half as many
successful dinner parties,

00:07:18.460 --> 00:07:20.050
I will be very grateful.

00:07:23.070 --> 00:07:26.700
Anyway, so after Bill
asked me to come up here,

00:07:26.700 --> 00:07:29.460
I realized-- this had not
occurred to me until then--

00:07:29.460 --> 00:07:34.170
but I realized that I mention
MIT in not one but two

00:07:34.170 --> 00:07:37.410
of the stories in my book.

00:07:37.410 --> 00:07:38.160
Go figure.

00:07:38.160 --> 00:07:40.650
I didn't study here.

00:07:40.650 --> 00:07:43.920
But I thought I'd read from one
of them in honor of my being

00:07:43.920 --> 00:07:44.490
here tonight.

00:07:44.490 --> 00:07:46.777
This one is called
"This Blessed House."

00:07:46.777 --> 00:07:47.860
I'll read the whole thing.

00:07:51.380 --> 00:07:55.040
They discovered the first one
in a cupboard above the stove,

00:07:55.040 --> 00:07:58.310
beside an unopened
bottle of malt vinegar.

00:07:58.310 --> 00:07:59.490
"Guess what I found?"

00:07:59.490 --> 00:08:00.980
Twinkle said.

00:08:00.980 --> 00:08:03.710
She walked into the living
room, lined from end

00:08:03.710 --> 00:08:06.190
to end with taped-up
packing boxes,

00:08:06.190 --> 00:08:09.440
waiving the vinegar in one
hand and a white porcelain

00:08:09.440 --> 00:08:12.590
effigy of Christ, roughly
the same size as the vinegar

00:08:12.590 --> 00:08:15.230
bottle, in the other.

00:08:15.230 --> 00:08:17.060
Sanjeev looked up.

00:08:17.060 --> 00:08:19.250
He was kneeling on
the floor, marking

00:08:19.250 --> 00:08:21.620
with ripped bits of
a Post-it patches

00:08:21.620 --> 00:08:24.670
on the baseboard that needed
to be retouched with paint.

00:08:24.670 --> 00:08:26.510
"Throw it away."

00:08:26.510 --> 00:08:27.720
"Which?"

00:08:27.720 --> 00:08:29.110
"Both."

00:08:29.110 --> 00:08:31.370
"But I can cook something
with the vinegar.

00:08:31.370 --> 00:08:33.450
It's brand new."

00:08:33.450 --> 00:08:36.350
"You've never cooked
anything with vinegar."

00:08:36.350 --> 00:08:38.549
"I'll look something up
in one of those books

00:08:38.549 --> 00:08:40.870
we got for our wedding."

00:08:40.870 --> 00:08:43.330
Sanjeev turned back
to the baseboard

00:08:43.330 --> 00:08:46.910
to replace a Post-it scrap
that had fallen to the floor.

00:08:46.910 --> 00:08:48.070
"Check the exploration.

00:08:48.070 --> 00:08:52.640
And at the very least, get
rid of that idiotic statue."

00:08:52.640 --> 00:08:54.470
"But it could be
worth something.

00:08:54.470 --> 00:08:55.880
Who knows?"

00:08:55.880 --> 00:08:59.540
She turned it upside down, then
stroked with her index finger

00:08:59.540 --> 00:09:02.600
the minuscule frozen
folds of its robes.

00:09:02.600 --> 00:09:04.520
"It's pretty."

00:09:04.520 --> 00:09:07.160
"We're not Christians,"
Sanjeev said.

00:09:07.160 --> 00:09:08.780
Lately he had begun
to notice the need

00:09:08.780 --> 00:09:10.550
to state the obvious to Twinkle.

00:09:10.550 --> 00:09:11.300
[LAUGHTER]

00:09:11.300 --> 00:09:13.070
The day before he
had to tell her

00:09:13.070 --> 00:09:14.840
that if she dragged
her end of the bureau

00:09:14.840 --> 00:09:18.470
instead of lifting it, the
parquet floor would scratch.

00:09:18.470 --> 00:09:19.760
She shrugged.

00:09:19.760 --> 00:09:21.740
"No, we're not Christian.

00:09:21.740 --> 00:09:23.990
We're good little Hindus."

00:09:23.990 --> 00:09:27.170
She planted a kiss on
top of Christ's head,

00:09:27.170 --> 00:09:30.090
then placed the statue on
top of the fireplace mantle,

00:09:30.090 --> 00:09:34.490
which needed, Sanjeev
observed, to be dusted.

00:09:34.490 --> 00:09:36.170
By the end of the
week the mantle

00:09:36.170 --> 00:09:38.000
had still not been dusted.

00:09:38.000 --> 00:09:40.190
It had, however, come
to serve as a display

00:09:40.190 --> 00:09:43.340
shelf for a sizable collection
of Christian paraphernalia.

00:09:43.340 --> 00:09:44.390
[LAUGHTER]

00:09:44.390 --> 00:09:47.090
There was a 3D postcard
of Saint Francis done

00:09:47.090 --> 00:09:49.250
in four colors, which
Twinkle had found

00:09:49.250 --> 00:09:51.650
taped to the back of
the medicine cabinet,

00:09:51.650 --> 00:09:54.860
and a wooden cross key chain
which Sanjeev had stepped on

00:09:54.860 --> 00:09:57.590
with bare feet as he was
installing extra shelving

00:09:57.590 --> 00:09:59.390
in Twinkle's study.

00:09:59.390 --> 00:10:01.280
There was a framed
paint-by-number

00:10:01.280 --> 00:10:05.120
of the three wise men against a
black velvet background tucked

00:10:05.120 --> 00:10:06.680
in the linen closet.

00:10:06.680 --> 00:10:09.080
There was also a
tile trivet depicting

00:10:09.080 --> 00:10:12.320
a blond, unbearded Jesus
delivering a sermon

00:10:12.320 --> 00:10:14.720
on a mountain top, left
in one of the drawers

00:10:14.720 --> 00:10:18.380
of the built-in china
cabinet in the dining room.

00:10:18.380 --> 00:10:20.800
"Do you think the previous
owners were born-agains?"

00:10:20.800 --> 00:10:23.060
asked Twinkle, making
room the next day

00:10:23.060 --> 00:10:26.690
for a small plastic
snow-filled dome containing

00:10:26.690 --> 00:10:30.050
a miniature nativity scene found
behind the pipes of the kitchen

00:10:30.050 --> 00:10:32.360
sink.

00:10:32.360 --> 00:10:34.640
Sanjeev was organizing
his engineering texts

00:10:34.640 --> 00:10:37.370
from MIT in alphabetical
order on a bookshelf--

00:10:37.370 --> 00:10:39.610
[LAUGHTER]

00:10:39.610 --> 00:10:41.530
though it had been
several years since he had

00:10:41.530 --> 00:10:44.020
needed to consult any of them.

00:10:44.020 --> 00:10:47.290
After graduating, he moved
from Boston to Connecticut

00:10:47.290 --> 00:10:49.420
to work for a firm
near Hartford.

00:10:49.420 --> 00:10:51.190
And he had recently
learned that he

00:10:51.190 --> 00:10:54.820
was being considered for the
position of vice president.

00:10:54.820 --> 00:10:58.120
At 33 he had a secretary of
his own and a dozen people

00:10:58.120 --> 00:11:01.450
working under his supervision,
who gladly supplied him

00:11:01.450 --> 00:11:03.820
with any information he needed.

00:11:03.820 --> 00:11:06.820
Still, the presence of his
college books in the room

00:11:06.820 --> 00:11:08.710
reminded him of a
time in his life

00:11:08.710 --> 00:11:10.780
he recalled with
fondness, when he

00:11:10.780 --> 00:11:13.810
would walk each evening
across the Mass Avenue Bridge

00:11:13.810 --> 00:11:16.390
in order to order mughlai
chicken with spinach

00:11:16.390 --> 00:11:18.970
from his favorite Indian
restaurant on the other side

00:11:18.970 --> 00:11:21.400
of the Charles, and
return to his dorm

00:11:21.400 --> 00:11:25.210
to write out clean copies
of his problem sets.

00:11:25.210 --> 00:11:29.380
"Or perhaps it's an attempt to
convert people," Twinkle mused.

00:11:29.380 --> 00:11:31.937
"Clearly the scheme has
succeeded in your case."

00:11:31.937 --> 00:11:33.130
[LAUGHTER]

00:11:33.130 --> 00:11:36.040
She disregarded him, shaking
the little plastic dome

00:11:36.040 --> 00:11:39.190
so that snow swirled
over the manger.

00:11:39.190 --> 00:11:41.680
He studied the
items on the mantle.

00:11:41.680 --> 00:11:45.310
It puzzled him that each was,
in its own way, so silly.

00:11:45.310 --> 00:11:48.190
Clearly they lacked a
sense of sacredness.

00:11:48.190 --> 00:11:51.250
He was further puzzled that
Twinkle, who normally displayed

00:11:51.250 --> 00:11:53.980
good taste, was so charmed.

00:11:53.980 --> 00:11:56.350
These objects meant
something to Twinkle,

00:11:56.350 --> 00:11:58.330
but they meant nothing to him.

00:11:58.330 --> 00:12:00.460
They irritated him.

00:12:00.460 --> 00:12:02.650
"We should call the
realtor, tell him there's

00:12:02.650 --> 00:12:04.680
all this nonsense left behind.

00:12:04.680 --> 00:12:06.790
Tell him to take it away."

00:12:06.790 --> 00:12:08.910
"Oh Sanj," Twinkle groaned.

00:12:08.910 --> 00:12:12.250
"Please, I would feel
terrible throwing them away.

00:12:12.250 --> 00:12:14.080
Obviously they were
important to the people

00:12:14.080 --> 00:12:15.400
who used to live here.

00:12:15.400 --> 00:12:16.480
It would feel--

00:12:16.480 --> 00:12:19.930
I don't know, sacrilegious
or something."

00:12:19.930 --> 00:12:21.520
"If they're so
precious, then why

00:12:21.520 --> 00:12:23.530
are they hidden
all over the house?

00:12:23.530 --> 00:12:26.250
Why didn't they take
them with them?"

00:12:26.250 --> 00:12:28.800
"There must be
others," Twinkle said.

00:12:28.800 --> 00:12:32.040
Her eyes roamed the bare
off-white walls of the room,

00:12:32.040 --> 00:12:35.490
as if there were other things
concealed behind the plaster.

00:12:35.490 --> 00:12:38.280
"What else do you
think we'll find?"

00:12:38.280 --> 00:12:40.950
But as they unpacked their
boxes and hung up their winter

00:12:40.950 --> 00:12:44.130
clothes and the silk paintings
of elephant processions

00:12:44.130 --> 00:12:47.280
bought on their honeymoon
in Jaipur, Twinkle,

00:12:47.280 --> 00:12:50.700
much to her dismay,
could not find a thing.

00:12:50.700 --> 00:12:53.730
Nearly a week had passed
before they discovered,

00:12:53.730 --> 00:12:57.000
one Saturday afternoon,
a larger-than-life-sized

00:12:57.000 --> 00:13:00.690
watercolor poster of Christ,
weeping translucent tears

00:13:00.690 --> 00:13:04.470
the size of peanut shells and
sporting a crown of thorns,

00:13:04.470 --> 00:13:07.770
rolled up behind a radiator
in the guest bedroom.

00:13:07.770 --> 00:13:11.550
Sanjeev had mistaken
it for a window shade.

00:13:11.550 --> 00:13:12.510
"Oh, we must!

00:13:12.510 --> 00:13:14.380
We simply must put it up.

00:13:14.380 --> 00:13:15.630
It's too spectacular."

00:13:15.630 --> 00:13:17.400
[LAUGHTER]

00:13:17.400 --> 00:13:19.260
Twinkle lit a
cigarette and began

00:13:19.260 --> 00:13:22.650
to smoke it with relish,
waving it around Sanjeev's head

00:13:22.650 --> 00:13:25.440
as if it were a conductor's
baton as Mahler's Fifth

00:13:25.440 --> 00:13:28.990
Symphony roared from
the stereo downstairs.

00:13:28.990 --> 00:13:30.220
"Now look.

00:13:30.220 --> 00:13:33.070
I will tolerate for now your
little biblical menagerie

00:13:33.070 --> 00:13:34.540
in the living room.

00:13:34.540 --> 00:13:37.270
But I refuse to
have this," he said,

00:13:37.270 --> 00:13:39.700
flicking at one of the
painted peanut tears,

00:13:39.700 --> 00:13:42.410
"displayed in our home."

00:13:42.410 --> 00:13:45.230
Twinkle stared at him,
placidly exhaling,

00:13:45.230 --> 00:13:49.220
the smoke emerging in two thin
blue streams from her nostrils.

00:13:49.220 --> 00:13:52.490
She rolled up the poster
slowly, securing it

00:13:52.490 --> 00:13:55.010
with one of the elastic
bands she always wore around

00:13:55.010 --> 00:13:58.520
her wrist for tying back
her thick, unruly hair,

00:13:58.520 --> 00:14:00.800
streaked here and
there with henna.

00:14:00.800 --> 00:14:03.710
"I'm going to put it in my
study," she informed him.

00:14:03.710 --> 00:14:06.680
"That way, you don't
have to look at it."

00:14:06.680 --> 00:14:08.110
"What about the house-warming?

00:14:08.110 --> 00:14:10.060
They'll want to
see all the rooms.

00:14:10.060 --> 00:14:12.430
I've invited people
from the office."

00:14:12.430 --> 00:14:14.080
She rolled her eyes.

00:14:14.080 --> 00:14:17.290
Sanjeev noted that the symphony,
now in its third movement,

00:14:17.290 --> 00:14:19.600
had reached a
crescendo, for it pulsed

00:14:19.600 --> 00:14:22.360
with the telltale
clashing of symbols.

00:14:22.360 --> 00:14:24.340
"I'll put it behind
the door," she offered.

00:14:24.340 --> 00:14:26.860
"That way, when they
peek in, they won't see.

00:14:26.860 --> 00:14:28.880
Happy?"

00:14:28.880 --> 00:14:31.670
He stood watching her as she
left the room with her poster

00:14:31.670 --> 00:14:33.140
and her cigarette.

00:14:33.140 --> 00:14:34.880
A few ashes had
fallen to the floor

00:14:34.880 --> 00:14:36.770
where she'd been standing.

00:14:36.770 --> 00:14:39.560
He bent down, pinched
them between his fingers,

00:14:39.560 --> 00:14:42.350
and deposited them
in his cupped palm.

00:14:42.350 --> 00:14:46.310
The tender fourth movement,
the adagiato, began.

00:14:46.310 --> 00:14:48.950
During breakfast Sanjeev
had read in the liner notes

00:14:48.950 --> 00:14:51.140
that Mahler had
proposed to his wife

00:14:51.140 --> 00:14:55.040
by sending her the manuscript
of this portion of the score.

00:14:55.040 --> 00:14:57.260
Although there were elements
of tragedy and struggle

00:14:57.260 --> 00:14:59.480
in the Fifth
Symphony, he had read,

00:14:59.480 --> 00:15:03.420
it was principally music
of love and happiness.

00:15:03.420 --> 00:15:05.730
He heard the toilet flush.

00:15:05.730 --> 00:15:09.510
"By the way," Twinkle hollered,
"if you want to impress people,

00:15:09.510 --> 00:15:10.900
I wouldn't play this music.

00:15:10.900 --> 00:15:12.482
It's putting me to sleep."

00:15:12.482 --> 00:15:13.750
[LAUGHTER]

00:15:13.750 --> 00:15:16.880
Sanjeev went to the bathroom
to throw away the ashes.

00:15:16.880 --> 00:15:19.540
The cigarette butt still
bobbed in the toilet bowl,

00:15:19.540 --> 00:15:21.010
but the tank was refilling.

00:15:21.010 --> 00:15:24.490
So he had to wait a moment
before he could flush it again.

00:15:24.490 --> 00:15:26.200
In the mirror of
the medicine cabinet

00:15:26.200 --> 00:15:28.360
he inspected his
long eyelashes--

00:15:28.360 --> 00:15:30.940
like a girl's, Twinkle
liked to tease.

00:15:30.940 --> 00:15:33.180
Though he was of average
build, his cheeks

00:15:33.180 --> 00:15:34.930
had a plumpness to them.

00:15:34.930 --> 00:15:37.900
This, along with the
eyelashes, detracted,

00:15:37.900 --> 00:15:42.040
he feared, from what he hoped
was a distinguished profile.

00:15:42.040 --> 00:15:44.770
He was of average height
as well, and wished ever

00:15:44.770 --> 00:15:47.350
since he had stopped
growing that he were just

00:15:47.350 --> 00:15:49.060
one inch taller.

00:15:49.060 --> 00:15:51.070
For this reason,
it irritated him

00:15:51.070 --> 00:15:53.704
when Twinkle insisted
on wearing high heels,

00:15:53.704 --> 00:15:55.870
as she had done the other
night when they ate dinner

00:15:55.870 --> 00:15:57.490
in Manhattan.

00:15:57.490 --> 00:16:00.670
This was the first weekend after
they'd moved into the house.

00:16:00.670 --> 00:16:03.670
By then the mantle had already
filled up considerably,

00:16:03.670 --> 00:16:07.090
and they had bickered about
it in the car on the way down.

00:16:07.090 --> 00:16:09.770
But then Twinkle had drunk
four glasses of whiskey

00:16:09.770 --> 00:16:13.820
in a nameless bar in Alphabet
City and forgot all about it.

00:16:13.820 --> 00:16:16.990
She dragged him to a tiny
bookshop on St. Mark's Place,

00:16:16.990 --> 00:16:19.300
where she browsed
for nearly an hour.

00:16:19.300 --> 00:16:20.950
And when they left
she insisted they

00:16:20.950 --> 00:16:24.940
dance a tango on the sidewalk,
in front of strangers.

00:16:24.940 --> 00:16:27.040
Afterwards, she
tottered on his arm,

00:16:27.040 --> 00:16:29.410
rising faintly over
his line of vision

00:16:29.410 --> 00:16:33.010
in a pair of suede, three-inch
leopard-print pumps.

00:16:33.010 --> 00:16:35.470
In this manner they walked
the endless blocks back

00:16:35.470 --> 00:16:38.260
to a parking garage
on Washington Square,

00:16:38.260 --> 00:16:40.570
for Sanjeev had heard
far too many stories

00:16:40.570 --> 00:16:44.410
about the terrible things that
happened to cars in Manhattan.

00:16:44.410 --> 00:16:46.810
"But I do nothing all day
except sit at my desk,"

00:16:46.810 --> 00:16:49.060
she fretted when they
were driving home,

00:16:49.060 --> 00:16:52.030
after he mentioned that her
shoes looked uncomfortable

00:16:52.030 --> 00:16:54.970
and suggested that perhaps
she should not wear them.

00:16:54.970 --> 00:16:58.190
"I can't exactly wear
heels when I'm typing."

00:16:58.190 --> 00:17:00.680
Though he abandoned the
argument, he knew for a fact

00:17:00.680 --> 00:17:02.840
that she didn't spend
all day at her desk.

00:17:02.840 --> 00:17:05.390
Just that afternoon when
he got back from a run,

00:17:05.390 --> 00:17:08.780
he found her inexplicably
in bed reading.

00:17:08.780 --> 00:17:11.599
When he asked her why she was
in bed in the middle of the day,

00:17:11.599 --> 00:17:13.910
she told him she was bored.

00:17:13.910 --> 00:17:15.589
He had wanted to
say to her then,

00:17:15.589 --> 00:17:17.200
"you could unpack some boxes.

00:17:17.200 --> 00:17:18.597
You could sweep the attic.

00:17:18.597 --> 00:17:20.930
You could retouch the paint
on the bathroom window sill.

00:17:20.930 --> 00:17:22.460
And after you do
it you can warn me,

00:17:22.460 --> 00:17:23.810
so I don't put my watch on it.

00:17:23.810 --> 00:17:25.270
[LAUGHTER]

00:17:25.270 --> 00:17:28.970
They didn't bother her, these
scattered, unsettled matters.

00:17:28.970 --> 00:17:30.710
She seemed content
with whatever clothes

00:17:30.710 --> 00:17:33.770
she found at the front of the
closet, with whatever magazine

00:17:33.770 --> 00:17:37.270
was lying around, with whatever
song was on the radio--

00:17:37.270 --> 00:17:39.860
content yet curious.

00:17:39.860 --> 00:17:41.930
And now all of her
curiosity centered

00:17:41.930 --> 00:17:43.550
around discovering
the next treasure.

00:17:46.330 --> 00:17:49.210
A few days later when Sanjeev
returned from the office,

00:17:49.210 --> 00:17:51.190
he found Twinkle
on the telephone,

00:17:51.190 --> 00:17:54.530
smoking and talking to one of
her girlfriends in California,

00:17:54.530 --> 00:17:56.500
even though it was
before five o'clock

00:17:56.500 --> 00:17:58.960
and the long-distance
rates were at their peak.

00:17:58.960 --> 00:18:00.130
[LAUGHTER]

00:18:00.130 --> 00:18:02.560
"Highly-devout people,"
she was saying,

00:18:02.560 --> 00:18:04.930
pausing every now
and then to exhale.

00:18:04.930 --> 00:18:06.820
Each day is like
a treasure hunt.

00:18:06.820 --> 00:18:07.990
I'm serious.

00:18:07.990 --> 00:18:09.257
This, you won't believe.

00:18:09.257 --> 00:18:11.215
The switch plates in the
bedroom were decorated

00:18:11.215 --> 00:18:12.970
with scenes from the Bible--

00:18:12.970 --> 00:18:15.280
you know, Noah's
ark and all that.

00:18:15.280 --> 00:18:19.120
Three bedrooms, but
one is my study.

00:18:19.120 --> 00:18:21.220
Sanjeev went to the
hardware store right away

00:18:21.220 --> 00:18:22.340
and replaced them.

00:18:22.340 --> 00:18:23.260
Can you imagine?

00:18:23.260 --> 00:18:26.180
He replaced every single one."

00:18:26.180 --> 00:18:28.390
Now it was the
friend's turn to talk.

00:18:28.390 --> 00:18:31.390
Twinkle nodded, slouched on the
floor in front of the fridge,

00:18:31.390 --> 00:18:34.870
wearing black stirrup pants
and a yellow chenille sweater,

00:18:34.870 --> 00:18:36.660
groping for her lighter.

00:18:36.660 --> 00:18:39.560
Sanjeev could smell something
aromatic on the stove,

00:18:39.560 --> 00:18:42.520
and he picked his way carefully
across the extra-long phone

00:18:42.520 --> 00:18:46.150
cord tangled on the
Mexican terracotta tiles.

00:18:46.150 --> 00:18:48.400
He opened the lid of
a pot with some sort

00:18:48.400 --> 00:18:51.430
of reddish-brown sauce
dripping over the sides,

00:18:51.430 --> 00:18:53.800
boiling furiously.

00:18:53.800 --> 00:18:55.750
"It's a stew I
made with the fish.

00:18:55.750 --> 00:18:57.690
I put the vinegar in
it," she said to him--

00:18:57.690 --> 00:18:58.190
[LAUGHTER]

00:18:58.190 --> 00:19:01.010
Interrupting her friend,
crossing her fingers.

00:19:01.010 --> 00:19:03.570
"Sorry, you were saying?"

00:19:03.570 --> 00:19:04.800
She was like that--

00:19:04.800 --> 00:19:07.020
excited and delighted
by little things,

00:19:07.020 --> 00:19:10.560
crossing her fingers before any
remotely unpredictable event,

00:19:10.560 --> 00:19:12.750
like tasting a new
flavor of ice cream

00:19:12.750 --> 00:19:15.210
or dropping a
letter in a mailbox.

00:19:15.210 --> 00:19:18.000
It was a quality he
did not understand.

00:19:18.000 --> 00:19:20.940
It made him feel stupid,
as if the world contained

00:19:20.940 --> 00:19:24.540
hidden wonders he could
not anticipate or see.

00:19:24.540 --> 00:19:27.780
He looked at her face
which, it occurred to him,

00:19:27.780 --> 00:19:29.850
had not grown out
of its girlhood,

00:19:29.850 --> 00:19:33.570
the eyes untroubled, the
pleasing features unfirm,

00:19:33.570 --> 00:19:35.790
as if they still had to
settle into some sort

00:19:35.790 --> 00:19:38.560
of permanent expression.

00:19:38.560 --> 00:19:41.110
Nicknamed after a nursery
rhyme, she had yet

00:19:41.110 --> 00:19:43.900
to shed a childhood endearment.

00:19:43.900 --> 00:19:46.330
Now, in the second
month of their marriage,

00:19:46.330 --> 00:19:48.250
certain things nettled him--

00:19:48.250 --> 00:19:49.930
the way she sometimes
spat a little

00:19:49.930 --> 00:19:52.390
when she spoke, or
left her undergarments,

00:19:52.390 --> 00:19:55.450
after removing them at night,
at the foot of their bed,

00:19:55.450 --> 00:19:59.590
rather than depositing
them in the laundry hamper.

00:19:59.590 --> 00:20:02.320
They had met only
four months before.

00:20:02.320 --> 00:20:04.210
Her parents, who
lived in California,

00:20:04.210 --> 00:20:08.380
and his, who still lived in
Calcutta, were old friends.

00:20:08.380 --> 00:20:10.180
And across continents,
they had arranged

00:20:10.180 --> 00:20:13.510
the occasion at which Twinkle
and Sanjeev were introduced--

00:20:13.510 --> 00:20:17.200
a 16th birthday party for a
daughter in their circle--

00:20:17.200 --> 00:20:20.710
when Sanjeev was in
Palo Alto on business.

00:20:20.710 --> 00:20:23.050
At the restaurant they
were seated side by side

00:20:23.050 --> 00:20:26.410
at a round table, with a
revolving platter of spare ribs

00:20:26.410 --> 00:20:29.470
and egg rolls and chicken
wings which, they concurred,

00:20:29.470 --> 00:20:31.180
all tasted the same.

00:20:31.180 --> 00:20:34.060
They had concurred, too, on
their adolescent but still

00:20:34.060 --> 00:20:36.760
persistent fondness
for Wodehouse novels

00:20:36.760 --> 00:20:38.770
and their dislike for the sitar.

00:20:38.770 --> 00:20:40.390
And later, Twinkle
confessed that she

00:20:40.390 --> 00:20:43.180
was charmed by the way
Sanjeev had dutifully

00:20:43.180 --> 00:20:47.020
refilled her teacup
during their conversation.

00:20:47.020 --> 00:20:50.030
And so the phone calls
began, and grew longer.

00:20:50.030 --> 00:20:51.100
And then the visits--

00:20:51.100 --> 00:20:54.130
first he to Stanford,
then she to Connecticut,

00:20:54.130 --> 00:20:56.110
after which Sanjeev
would save in an ash

00:20:56.110 --> 00:20:58.750
tray left on the balcony
the crushed cigarettes

00:20:58.750 --> 00:21:00.880
she had smoked
during the weekend.

00:21:00.880 --> 00:21:03.220
Saved them, that is,
until the next time

00:21:03.220 --> 00:21:04.720
she came to visit him.

00:21:04.720 --> 00:21:07.600
And then he vacuumed the
apartment, washed the sheets,

00:21:07.600 --> 00:21:10.540
even dusted the plant
leaves in her honor.

00:21:10.540 --> 00:21:13.480
She was 27 and
recently abandoned,

00:21:13.480 --> 00:21:16.420
he gathered, by an American
who had tried and failed

00:21:16.420 --> 00:21:17.830
to be an actor.

00:21:17.830 --> 00:21:21.040
Sanjeev was lonely, with an
excessively generous income

00:21:21.040 --> 00:21:24.880
for a single man, and
had never been in love.

00:21:24.880 --> 00:21:26.470
At the urging of
their matchmakers

00:21:26.470 --> 00:21:29.440
they married in India, amid
hundreds of well-wishers

00:21:29.440 --> 00:21:31.940
whom he barely remembered
from his childhood,

00:21:31.940 --> 00:21:36.040
in incessant August rains under
a red and orange tent strung

00:21:36.040 --> 00:21:40.200
with Christmas tree lights
on [? Mandavil ?] Road.

00:21:40.200 --> 00:21:42.830
"Did you sweep the attic?"
he asked Twinkle later,

00:21:42.830 --> 00:21:45.240
as she was folding paper
napkins and wedging them

00:21:45.240 --> 00:21:46.680
by their plates.

00:21:46.680 --> 00:21:49.140
The attic was the only part
of the house they had not yet

00:21:49.140 --> 00:21:51.300
given an initial cleaning.

00:21:51.300 --> 00:21:52.020
"Not yet.

00:21:52.020 --> 00:21:53.460
I promise, I will.

00:21:53.460 --> 00:21:55.320
I hope this tastes
good," she said,

00:21:55.320 --> 00:21:58.860
planting the steaming pot
on top of the Jesus trivet.

00:21:58.860 --> 00:22:01.680
There was a loaf of Italian
bread in a little basket,

00:22:01.680 --> 00:22:03.600
and iceberg lettuce
and grated carrots

00:22:03.600 --> 00:22:06.510
topped with bottled dressing
and croutons, and glasses

00:22:06.510 --> 00:22:08.070
of red wine.

00:22:08.070 --> 00:22:11.050
She was not terribly
ambitious in the kitchen.

00:22:11.050 --> 00:22:13.770
She bought pre-roasted
chickens from the supermarket

00:22:13.770 --> 00:22:17.310
and served them with potato
salad, prepared who knew when,

00:22:17.310 --> 00:22:19.890
sold in little
plastic containers.

00:22:19.890 --> 00:22:22.620
Indian food, she
complained, was a bother.

00:22:22.620 --> 00:22:25.470
She detested chopping
garlic and peeling ginger,

00:22:25.470 --> 00:22:27.720
and could not operate a blender.

00:22:27.720 --> 00:22:30.550
And so it was Sanjeev
who, on weekends,

00:22:30.550 --> 00:22:32.220
seasoned mustard
oil with cinnamon

00:22:32.220 --> 00:22:36.750
sticks and cloves in order
to produce a proper curry.

00:22:36.750 --> 00:22:38.760
He had to admit,
though, that whatever

00:22:38.760 --> 00:22:42.300
it was that she had cooked
today, it was unusually tasty--

00:22:42.300 --> 00:22:45.690
attractive, even, with
bright white cubes of fish

00:22:45.690 --> 00:22:48.240
and flecks of parsley
and fresh tomatoes

00:22:48.240 --> 00:22:51.480
gleaming in the
dark-brown red broth.

00:22:51.480 --> 00:22:52.980
"How did you make it?"

00:22:52.980 --> 00:22:54.450
"I made it up."

00:22:54.450 --> 00:22:56.010
"What did you do?"

00:22:56.010 --> 00:22:57.540
"I just put some
things into the pot

00:22:57.540 --> 00:22:59.164
and added the malt
vinegar at the end."

00:22:59.164 --> 00:23:00.540
[LAUGHTER]

00:23:00.540 --> 00:23:01.950
"How much vinegar?"

00:23:01.950 --> 00:23:03.900
She shrugged, ripping
off some bread

00:23:03.900 --> 00:23:06.120
and plunging it into her bowl.

00:23:06.120 --> 00:23:07.740
"What do you mean,
you don't know?

00:23:07.740 --> 00:23:09.030
You should write it down.

00:23:09.030 --> 00:23:10.860
What if you need
to make it again,

00:23:10.860 --> 00:23:12.720
for a party or something?"

00:23:12.720 --> 00:23:14.400
"I'll remember," she said.

00:23:14.400 --> 00:23:17.970
She covered the bread basket
with a dish towel that had,

00:23:17.970 --> 00:23:21.237
he suddenly noticed, the 10
commandments printed on it.

00:23:21.237 --> 00:23:22.670
[LAUGHTER]

00:23:22.670 --> 00:23:25.400
She flashed him a little
smile, giving his knee

00:23:25.400 --> 00:23:27.350
a little squeeze
under the table.

00:23:27.350 --> 00:23:29.735
"Face it-- this
house is blessed."

00:23:29.735 --> 00:23:33.920
[LAUGHTER]

00:23:33.920 --> 00:23:35.570
The house-warming
party was scheduled

00:23:35.570 --> 00:23:37.970
for the last
Saturday in October,

00:23:37.970 --> 00:23:40.790
and they had invited
about 30 people.

00:23:40.790 --> 00:23:42.990
All were Sanjeev's
acquaintances,

00:23:42.990 --> 00:23:44.930
people from the
office and a number

00:23:44.930 --> 00:23:48.020
of Indian couples in the
Connecticut area, many of whom

00:23:48.020 --> 00:23:50.300
he barely knew, but
who had regularly

00:23:50.300 --> 00:23:54.650
invited him in his bachelor
days to supper on Saturdays.

00:23:54.650 --> 00:23:57.770
He often wondered why they
included him in their circle.

00:23:57.770 --> 00:24:01.690
He had little in common
with any of them.

00:24:01.690 --> 00:24:03.830
But he always attended
their gatherings,

00:24:03.830 --> 00:24:07.100
to eat spiced chickpeas and
shrimp cutlets, and gossip

00:24:07.100 --> 00:24:11.090
and discuss politics, for
he seldom had other plans.

00:24:11.090 --> 00:24:13.490
So far, no one had met Twinkle.

00:24:13.490 --> 00:24:15.290
Back when they
were still dating,

00:24:15.290 --> 00:24:17.840
Sanjeev didn't want to waste
their brief weekends together

00:24:17.840 --> 00:24:21.170
with people he associated
with being alone.

00:24:21.170 --> 00:24:24.050
Other than Sanjeev and an
ex-boyfriend, who she believed

00:24:24.050 --> 00:24:26.750
worked in a pottery
studio in Brookfield,

00:24:26.750 --> 00:24:29.330
she knew no one in the
state of Connecticut.

00:24:29.330 --> 00:24:31.150
She was completing
her master's thesis

00:24:31.150 --> 00:24:34.040
at Stanford, a study
of an Irish poet

00:24:34.040 --> 00:24:37.340
whom Sanjeev had never heard of.

00:24:37.340 --> 00:24:39.620
Sanjeev had found
the house on his own,

00:24:39.620 --> 00:24:42.440
before leaving for the
wedding, for a good price

00:24:42.440 --> 00:24:45.290
in a neighborhood with
a fine school system.

00:24:45.290 --> 00:24:48.140
He was impressed by the
elegant curved staircase

00:24:48.140 --> 00:24:50.990
with its wrought iron
banister, and the dark wooden

00:24:50.990 --> 00:24:54.260
wainscotting, and the solarium
overlooking rhododendron

00:24:54.260 --> 00:24:57.560
bushes, and the
solid brass 22, which

00:24:57.560 --> 00:24:59.930
also happened to be
the date of his birth,

00:24:59.930 --> 00:25:03.550
nailed impressively to
the vaguely Tudor facade.

00:25:03.550 --> 00:25:06.640
There were two working
fireplaces, a two-car garage,

00:25:06.640 --> 00:25:09.730
and an attic suitable for
converting into extra bedrooms

00:25:09.730 --> 00:25:13.630
if, the realtor mentioned,
the need should arise.

00:25:13.630 --> 00:25:16.302
By then Sanjeev had
already made up his mind,

00:25:16.302 --> 00:25:18.010
was determined that
he and Twinkle should

00:25:18.010 --> 00:25:20.230
live there together forever.

00:25:20.230 --> 00:25:21.880
And so he had not
bothered to notice

00:25:21.880 --> 00:25:24.610
the switch plates covered
with biblical stickers,

00:25:24.610 --> 00:25:27.740
or the transparent decal of
the Virgin on a half shell,

00:25:27.740 --> 00:25:30.339
as Twinkle liked to call
it, adhered to the window

00:25:30.339 --> 00:25:31.255
in the master bedroom.

00:25:31.255 --> 00:25:32.530
[LAUGHTER]

00:25:32.530 --> 00:25:35.830
When, after moving in, he
tried to scrape it off,

00:25:35.830 --> 00:25:36.970
he scratched the glass.

00:25:40.380 --> 00:25:41.820
The weekend before
the party they

00:25:41.820 --> 00:25:44.910
were raking the lawn when
he heard Twinkle shriek.

00:25:44.910 --> 00:25:47.580
He ran to her,
clutching his rake,

00:25:47.580 --> 00:25:51.060
worried that she had discovered
a dead animal or a snake.

00:25:51.060 --> 00:25:53.790
A brisk October breeze
stung the tops of his ears

00:25:53.790 --> 00:25:57.090
as his sneakers crunched
over brown and yellow leaves.

00:25:57.090 --> 00:25:58.650
When he reached her
she had collapsed

00:25:58.650 --> 00:26:02.520
on the grass, dissolved
in nearly silent laughter.

00:26:02.520 --> 00:26:04.980
Behind an overgrown
forsythia bush

00:26:04.980 --> 00:26:07.780
was a plaster Virgin Mary
as tall as their waists,

00:26:07.780 --> 00:26:11.250
with a blue painted hood
draped over her head,

00:26:11.250 --> 00:26:13.950
in the manner of
an Indian bride.

00:26:13.950 --> 00:26:16.230
Twinkle grabbed at
the hem of her t-shirt

00:26:16.230 --> 00:26:20.740
and began wiping away the dirt
staining this statue's brow.

00:26:20.740 --> 00:26:23.080
"I suppose you want to put
her by the foot of our bed,"

00:26:23.080 --> 00:26:23.650
Sanjeev said.

00:26:23.650 --> 00:26:25.330
[LAUGHTER]

00:26:25.330 --> 00:26:27.430
She looked at him, astonished.

00:26:27.430 --> 00:26:29.410
Her belly was
exposed, and he saw

00:26:29.410 --> 00:26:31.900
that there were goosebumps
around her navel.

00:26:31.900 --> 00:26:33.100
"What do you think?

00:26:33.100 --> 00:26:36.050
Of course we can't put
this in our bedroom."

00:26:36.050 --> 00:26:37.230
"We can't?"

00:26:37.230 --> 00:26:38.960
"No, silly Sanj.

00:26:38.960 --> 00:26:40.856
This is meant for
outside, for the lawn.

00:26:40.856 --> 00:26:43.090
[LAUGHTER]

00:26:43.090 --> 00:26:45.070
"Oh god, no.

00:26:45.070 --> 00:26:46.405
Twinkle, no."

00:26:46.405 --> 00:26:47.740
"But we must.

00:26:47.740 --> 00:26:50.500
It would be bad luck not to."

00:26:50.500 --> 00:26:51.880
"All the neighbors will see.

00:26:51.880 --> 00:26:53.230
They'll think we're insane."

00:26:53.230 --> 00:26:54.560
[LAUGHTER]

00:26:54.560 --> 00:26:55.150
"Why?

00:26:55.150 --> 00:26:57.996
For having a statue of the
Virgin Mary on our lawn?

00:26:57.996 --> 00:26:59.620
Every other person
in this neighborhood

00:26:59.620 --> 00:27:01.480
has a statue of
Mary on the lawn.

00:27:01.480 --> 00:27:02.680
We'll fit right in."

00:27:02.680 --> 00:27:04.630
[LAUGHTER]

00:27:04.630 --> 00:27:06.430
"We are not Christian."

00:27:06.430 --> 00:27:08.350
"So you keep reminding me."

00:27:08.350 --> 00:27:10.330
She spat onto the
tip of her finger

00:27:10.330 --> 00:27:13.750
and started to rub intently at
a particularly stubborn stain

00:27:13.750 --> 00:27:15.150
on Mary's chin.

00:27:15.150 --> 00:27:17.380
"Do you think this is dirt,
or some kind of fungus?"

00:27:17.380 --> 00:27:19.300
[LAUGHTER]

00:27:19.300 --> 00:27:21.850
He was getting nowhere
with her, with this woman

00:27:21.850 --> 00:27:23.710
whom he had known
only for four months

00:27:23.710 --> 00:27:26.500
and whom he had married,
this woman with whom he now

00:27:26.500 --> 00:27:28.330
shared his life.

00:27:28.330 --> 00:27:30.100
He thought, with a
flicker of regret,

00:27:30.100 --> 00:27:33.450
of the snapshots his mother
used to send him from Calcutta

00:27:33.450 --> 00:27:36.160
of prospective brides
who could sing and sew,

00:27:36.160 --> 00:27:38.650
and season lentils without
consulting a cookbook.

00:27:38.650 --> 00:27:39.830
[LAUGHTER]

00:27:39.830 --> 00:27:42.030
Sanjeev had considered
these women,

00:27:42.030 --> 00:27:45.400
and even ranked them
in order of preference,

00:27:45.400 --> 00:27:47.500
but then he had met Twinkle.

00:27:47.500 --> 00:27:50.410
"Twinkle, I can't have
the people I work with

00:27:50.410 --> 00:27:52.995
see this statue on my lawn."

00:27:52.995 --> 00:27:54.745
"They can't fire you
for being a believer.

00:27:54.745 --> 00:27:55.245
[LAUGHTER]

00:27:55.245 --> 00:27:57.610
It would be discrimination."

00:27:57.610 --> 00:27:59.410
"That's not the point."

00:27:59.410 --> 00:28:02.740
"Why does it matter to you so
much what other people think?"

00:28:02.740 --> 00:28:04.540
"Twinkle, please."

00:28:04.540 --> 00:28:05.980
He was tired.

00:28:05.980 --> 00:28:08.260
He let his weight
rest against his rake

00:28:08.260 --> 00:28:11.830
as she began dragging the statue
toward an oval bed of myrtle

00:28:11.830 --> 00:28:14.770
beside the lamppost that
flanked the brick pathway.

00:28:14.770 --> 00:28:17.920
"Look, Sanj, she's so lovely."

00:28:17.920 --> 00:28:19.510
He returned to
his pile of leaves

00:28:19.510 --> 00:28:22.720
and began to deposit them by
handfuls into a plastic garbage

00:28:22.720 --> 00:28:23.860
bag.

00:28:23.860 --> 00:28:26.880
Over his head, the
blue sky was cloudless.

00:28:26.880 --> 00:28:30.790
One tree on the lawn was still
full of leaves, red and orange,

00:28:30.790 --> 00:28:34.090
like the tent in which
he had married Twinkle.

00:28:34.090 --> 00:28:36.370
He did not know if he loved her.

00:28:36.370 --> 00:28:40.210
He said he did, when she first
asked him one afternoon in Palo

00:28:40.210 --> 00:28:43.900
Alto, as they sat side by
side in a darkened, nearly

00:28:43.900 --> 00:28:45.790
empty movie theater.

00:28:45.790 --> 00:28:48.430
Before the film, one
of her favorites--

00:28:48.430 --> 00:28:51.580
something in German that he
found extremely depressing--

00:28:51.580 --> 00:28:53.170
she had pressed
the tip of her nose

00:28:53.170 --> 00:28:55.390
to his, so that he
could feel the flutter

00:28:55.390 --> 00:28:58.270
of her mascara-coated eyelashes.

00:28:58.270 --> 00:29:01.690
That afternoon he had
replied, yes, he loved her.

00:29:01.690 --> 00:29:04.900
And she was delighted, and
fed him a piece of popcorn,

00:29:04.900 --> 00:29:09.010
letting her finger linger
an instant between his lips,

00:29:09.010 --> 00:29:10.870
as if it were his
reward for coming up

00:29:10.870 --> 00:29:13.210
with the right answer.

00:29:13.210 --> 00:29:15.130
Though she did not
say it herself,

00:29:15.130 --> 00:29:17.410
he assumed that
she loved him too.

00:29:17.410 --> 00:29:19.485
But now he was no longer sure.

00:29:19.485 --> 00:29:23.470
In truth, Sanjeev did not
know what love was, only

00:29:23.470 --> 00:29:25.010
what he thought it was not.

00:29:25.010 --> 00:29:27.730
It was not, he had
decided, returning

00:29:27.730 --> 00:29:30.430
to an empty carpeted
condominium each night,

00:29:30.430 --> 00:29:33.640
and using only the top
fork in his cutlery drawer,

00:29:33.640 --> 00:29:35.980
and turning away politely
at those weekend dinner

00:29:35.980 --> 00:29:38.020
parties when the
other man eventually

00:29:38.020 --> 00:29:41.260
put their arms around the waists
of their wives and girlfriends,

00:29:41.260 --> 00:29:44.030
leaning over every now and
then to kiss their shoulders

00:29:44.030 --> 00:29:45.370
or necks.

00:29:45.370 --> 00:29:49.180
It was not sending away for
classical musical CDs by mail,

00:29:49.180 --> 00:29:52.210
working his way methodically
through the major composers

00:29:52.210 --> 00:29:55.240
that the catalog recommended,
and always sending his payments

00:29:55.240 --> 00:29:57.070
in on time.

00:29:57.070 --> 00:30:00.410
In the months before
meeting Twinkle,

00:30:00.410 --> 00:30:03.361
Sanjeev had begun
to realize this.

00:30:03.361 --> 00:30:05.860
"You have enough money in the
bank to raise three families,"

00:30:05.860 --> 00:30:07.360
his mother reminded
him when they

00:30:07.360 --> 00:30:09.850
spoke at the start of
each month on the phone.

00:30:09.850 --> 00:30:12.940
"You need a wife to
look after and love."

00:30:12.940 --> 00:30:16.810
Now he had one, a pretty one
from a suitably high caste, who

00:30:16.810 --> 00:30:18.755
would soon have a
master's degree.

00:30:18.755 --> 00:30:20.710
What was there not to love?

00:30:23.560 --> 00:30:26.710
That evening, Sanjeev poured
himself a gin and tonic,

00:30:26.710 --> 00:30:30.190
drank it and most of another
during one segment of the news,

00:30:30.190 --> 00:30:33.240
and then approached Twinkle,
who was taking a bubble bath,

00:30:33.240 --> 00:30:36.160
for she announced that her limbs
ached from raking the lawn--

00:30:36.160 --> 00:30:38.440
something she had
never done before.

00:30:38.440 --> 00:30:40.150
He didn't knock.

00:30:40.150 --> 00:30:42.880
She had applied a bright
blue mask to her face,

00:30:42.880 --> 00:30:45.670
was smoking and sipping
some bourbon with ice,

00:30:45.670 --> 00:30:47.320
and leafing through
a fat paperback

00:30:47.320 --> 00:30:51.400
book whose pages had buckled
and turned gray from the water.

00:30:51.400 --> 00:30:52.840
He glanced at the cover.

00:30:52.840 --> 00:30:55.530
The only thing written on
it was the word "Sonnets"

00:30:55.530 --> 00:30:57.670
in dark red letters.

00:30:57.670 --> 00:31:00.880
He took a breath, and then
he informed her very calmly

00:31:00.880 --> 00:31:02.460
that after finishing
his drink, he

00:31:02.460 --> 00:31:05.440
was going to put on his shoes
and go outside and remove

00:31:05.440 --> 00:31:08.500
the Virgin from the front lawn.

00:31:08.500 --> 00:31:10.120
"Where are you going
to put it?" she

00:31:10.120 --> 00:31:13.000
asked him dreamily,
her eyes closed.

00:31:13.000 --> 00:31:15.820
One of her legs emerged,
unfolding gracefully

00:31:15.820 --> 00:31:17.590
from the layer of suds.

00:31:17.590 --> 00:31:20.290
She flexed and pointed her toes.

00:31:20.290 --> 00:31:22.990
"For now I'm going to
put it in the garage.

00:31:22.990 --> 00:31:25.560
Then tomorrow morning
on my way to work,

00:31:25.560 --> 00:31:28.420
I'm going to take
it to the dump."

00:31:28.420 --> 00:31:30.130
"Don't you dare."

00:31:30.130 --> 00:31:33.730
She stood up, letting the book
fall into the water, bubbles

00:31:33.730 --> 00:31:36.010
dripping down her thighs.

00:31:36.010 --> 00:31:39.670
"I hate you," she informed him,
her eyes narrowing at the word

00:31:39.670 --> 00:31:40.930
hate.

00:31:40.930 --> 00:31:42.940
She reached for her
bathrobe, tied it

00:31:42.940 --> 00:31:45.280
tightly about her
waist, and padded down

00:31:45.280 --> 00:31:48.280
the winding staircase,
leaving sloppy wet footprints

00:31:48.280 --> 00:31:50.730
along the parquet floor.

00:31:50.730 --> 00:31:53.190
When she reached the
foyer Sanjeev said,

00:31:53.190 --> 00:31:56.070
"are you planning on
leaving the house that way?"

00:31:56.070 --> 00:31:58.050
He felt a throbbing
in his temples,

00:31:58.050 --> 00:32:01.950
and his voice revealed an
unfamiliar snarl when he spoke.

00:32:01.950 --> 00:32:02.980
"Who cares?

00:32:02.980 --> 00:32:05.520
Who cares what way
I leave this house?"

00:32:05.520 --> 00:32:08.100
"Where are you planning
on going at this hour?"

00:32:08.100 --> 00:32:09.780
"You can't throw
away that statue.

00:32:09.780 --> 00:32:11.370
I won't let you."

00:32:11.370 --> 00:32:14.730
Her mask, now dry, had
assumed an ashen quality,

00:32:14.730 --> 00:32:17.670
and water from her hair
dripped onto the caked contours

00:32:17.670 --> 00:32:18.990
of her face.

00:32:18.990 --> 00:32:20.130
"Yes I can.

00:32:20.130 --> 00:32:21.450
I will."

00:32:21.450 --> 00:32:24.990
"No," Twinkle said, her
voice suddenly small.

00:32:24.990 --> 00:32:26.490
This is our house.

00:32:26.490 --> 00:32:28.050
We own it together.

00:32:28.050 --> 00:32:31.000
The statue was a
part of our property.

00:32:31.000 --> 00:32:32.530
She had begun to shiver.

00:32:32.530 --> 00:32:36.070
A small pool of bath water had
collected around her ankles.

00:32:36.070 --> 00:32:37.840
He went to shut
a window, fearing

00:32:37.840 --> 00:32:39.610
that she would catch cold.

00:32:39.610 --> 00:32:41.800
Then he noticed that some
of the water dripping down

00:32:41.800 --> 00:32:44.770
her hard blue face was tears.

00:32:44.770 --> 00:32:46.600
"Oh god, Twinkle, please--

00:32:46.600 --> 00:32:48.190
I didn't mean it."

00:32:48.190 --> 00:32:51.010
He had never seen her cry
before, had never seen

00:32:51.010 --> 00:32:53.050
such sadness in her eyes.

00:32:53.050 --> 00:32:55.780
She didn't turn away or
try to stop the tears.

00:32:55.780 --> 00:32:58.630
Instead, she looked
strangely at peace.

00:32:58.630 --> 00:33:01.930
For a moment she closed her
lids, pale and unprotected

00:33:01.930 --> 00:33:05.110
compared to the blue that
caked the rest of her face.

00:33:05.110 --> 00:33:07.540
Sanjeev felt ill,
as if he had eaten

00:33:07.540 --> 00:33:10.300
either too much or too little.

00:33:10.300 --> 00:33:13.990
She went to him, placing
her damp toweled arms

00:33:13.990 --> 00:33:18.070
about his neck, sobbing into
his chest, soaking his shirt.

00:33:18.070 --> 00:33:21.170
The mask flaked
onto his shoulders.

00:33:21.170 --> 00:33:23.780
In the end, they
settled on a compromise.

00:33:23.780 --> 00:33:25.730
The statue would be
placed in a recess

00:33:25.730 --> 00:33:28.010
at the side of the
house, so that it wasn't

00:33:28.010 --> 00:33:31.850
obvious to passers by, but
was still clearly visible

00:33:31.850 --> 00:33:32.690
to all who came.

00:33:36.520 --> 00:33:39.340
The menu for the party
was fairly simple.

00:33:39.340 --> 00:33:41.260
There would be a
case of champagne,

00:33:41.260 --> 00:33:43.960
and samosas from an Indian
restaurant in Hartford,

00:33:43.960 --> 00:33:46.690
and big trays of rice with
chicken and almonds and orange

00:33:46.690 --> 00:33:49.450
peels, which Sanjeev had spent
the greater part of the morning

00:33:49.450 --> 00:33:51.730
and afternoon preparing.

00:33:51.730 --> 00:33:54.460
He had never entertained on
such a large scale before

00:33:54.460 --> 00:33:57.160
and, worried that there
would not be enough to drink,

00:33:57.160 --> 00:33:58.870
ran out at one point
to buy another case

00:33:58.870 --> 00:34:00.970
of champagne just in case.

00:34:00.970 --> 00:34:03.340
For this reason he burned
one of the rice trays,

00:34:03.340 --> 00:34:05.590
and had to start it over again.

00:34:05.590 --> 00:34:07.700
Twinkle swept the
floors, and volunteered

00:34:07.700 --> 00:34:09.269
to pick up the samosas.

00:34:09.269 --> 00:34:10.810
She had an appointment
for a manicure

00:34:10.810 --> 00:34:13.949
and a pedicure in
that direction anyway.

00:34:13.949 --> 00:34:16.120
Sanjeev had planned to
ask if she would consider

00:34:16.120 --> 00:34:20.580
clearing the menagerie off the
mantle, if only for the party.

00:34:20.580 --> 00:34:23.199
But she had left while
he was in the shower.

00:34:23.199 --> 00:34:25.600
She was gone for a
good three hours,

00:34:25.600 --> 00:34:28.840
and so it was Sanjeev who
did the rest of the cleaning.

00:34:28.840 --> 00:34:32.630
By 5:30 the entire house
sparkled, with scented candles

00:34:32.630 --> 00:34:34.960
that Twinkle had picked up
in Hartford illuminating

00:34:34.960 --> 00:34:37.659
the items on the mantle,
and slender stalks

00:34:37.659 --> 00:34:43.040
of burning incense planted
into the soil of potted plants.

00:34:43.040 --> 00:34:46.340
Each time he passed the mantle
he winced, dreading the raised

00:34:46.340 --> 00:34:48.139
eyebrows of his
guests as they viewed

00:34:48.139 --> 00:34:50.449
the flickering ceramic
saints, the salt

00:34:50.449 --> 00:34:53.120
and pepper shakers designed
to resemble Mary and Joseph.

00:34:53.120 --> 00:34:54.139
[LAUGHTER]

00:34:54.139 --> 00:34:57.920
Still, they would be impressed,
he hoped, by the lovely bay

00:34:57.920 --> 00:35:00.380
windows and shining
parquet floors,

00:35:00.380 --> 00:35:02.210
the impressive
winding staircase,

00:35:02.210 --> 00:35:06.410
the wooden wainscotting, as
they sipped champagne and dipped

00:35:06.410 --> 00:35:09.710
samosas into chutney.

00:35:09.710 --> 00:35:12.440
Douglas, one of the new
consultants at the firm,

00:35:12.440 --> 00:35:15.440
and his girlfriend Nora
were the first to arrive.

00:35:15.440 --> 00:35:17.540
Both were tall
and blond, wearing

00:35:17.540 --> 00:35:21.290
matching wire-rimmed glasses
and long black overcoats.

00:35:21.290 --> 00:35:24.500
Nora wore a black hat full
of sharp thin feathers

00:35:24.500 --> 00:35:28.040
that corresponded to the
sharp thin angles of her face.

00:35:28.040 --> 00:35:30.590
Her left hand was
joined with Douglas's.

00:35:30.590 --> 00:35:32.840
In her right hand was
a bottle of cognac

00:35:32.840 --> 00:35:35.210
with a red ribbon wrapped
around its neck, which

00:35:35.210 --> 00:35:37.100
she gave to Twinkle.

00:35:37.100 --> 00:35:39.920
"Great lawn, Sanjeev,"
Douglas remarked.

00:35:39.920 --> 00:35:43.030
We've got to get that rake
out ourselves, sweetie.

00:35:43.030 --> 00:35:46.940
And this must be--" "My
wife, [? Donima." ?]

00:35:46.940 --> 00:35:48.460
"Call me Twinkle."

00:35:48.460 --> 00:35:50.660
"What an unusual
name," Nora remarked.

00:35:50.660 --> 00:35:51.710
Twinkle shrugged.

00:35:51.710 --> 00:35:52.670
"Not really.

00:35:52.670 --> 00:35:55.337
There's an actress in
Bombay named Dimple Kapadia.

00:35:55.337 --> 00:35:56.795
She even has a
sister named Simple.

00:35:56.795 --> 00:35:59.320
[LAUGHTER]

00:35:59.320 --> 00:36:02.570
Douglas and Nora raised their
eyebrows simultaneously,

00:36:02.570 --> 00:36:05.570
nodding slowly, as if to let
the absurdity of the name

00:36:05.570 --> 00:36:07.040
settle in.

00:36:07.040 --> 00:36:09.290
"Pleased to meet you, Twinkle."

00:36:09.290 --> 00:36:10.810
"Help yourself to champagne.

00:36:10.810 --> 00:36:13.100
There's gallons."

00:36:13.100 --> 00:36:15.710
"I hope you don't mind
my asking," Douglas said,

00:36:15.710 --> 00:36:17.720
"but I noticed a
statue outside, and--"

00:36:17.720 --> 00:36:18.626
[LAUGHTER]

00:36:18.626 --> 00:36:20.330
"Are you guys Christian?

00:36:20.330 --> 00:36:22.550
I thought you were Indian."

00:36:22.550 --> 00:36:25.580
"There are Christians in
India," Sanjeev replied,

00:36:25.580 --> 00:36:27.680
"but we are not."

00:36:27.680 --> 00:36:30.720
"I love your outfit,"
Nora told Twinkle.

00:36:30.720 --> 00:36:32.070
"And I adore your hat.

00:36:32.070 --> 00:36:35.030
Would you like the grand tour?"

00:36:35.030 --> 00:36:37.940
The bell rang again,
and again, and again.

00:36:37.940 --> 00:36:39.440
Within minutes, it
seemed, the house

00:36:39.440 --> 00:36:41.480
had filled with bodies
and conversations

00:36:41.480 --> 00:36:43.740
and unfamiliar fragrances.

00:36:43.740 --> 00:36:46.280
The women wore heels
and sheer stockings,

00:36:46.280 --> 00:36:49.970
and short black dresses
made of crepe and chiffon.

00:36:49.970 --> 00:36:51.470
They handed their
wraps and coats

00:36:51.470 --> 00:36:54.350
to Sanjeev, who draped
them carefully on hangers

00:36:54.350 --> 00:36:57.620
in the spacious coat closet,
though Twinkle told people

00:36:57.620 --> 00:37:01.070
to throw their things on the
ottomans in the solarium.

00:37:01.070 --> 00:37:03.890
Some of the Indian women
wore their finest saris,

00:37:03.890 --> 00:37:06.770
made with gold filigree that
draped in elegant pleats

00:37:06.770 --> 00:37:08.360
over their shoulders.

00:37:08.360 --> 00:37:12.800
The men wore jackets and ties
and citrus-scented aftershaves.

00:37:12.800 --> 00:37:15.350
As people filtered from
one room to the next,

00:37:15.350 --> 00:37:17.930
presents piles onto the
long cherrywood table

00:37:17.930 --> 00:37:21.950
that ran from one end of the
downstairs hall to the other.

00:37:21.950 --> 00:37:23.570
It bewildered
Sanjeev that it was

00:37:23.570 --> 00:37:26.570
for him and his
house and his wife

00:37:26.570 --> 00:37:29.360
that they had all
gone to so much care.

00:37:29.360 --> 00:37:31.790
The only other time in his
life that something similar had

00:37:31.790 --> 00:37:33.590
happened was his wedding.

00:37:33.590 --> 00:37:36.020
But somehow this was
different, for these were not

00:37:36.020 --> 00:37:38.300
his family but people
who knew him only

00:37:38.300 --> 00:37:42.110
casually and, in a
sense, owed him nothing.

00:37:42.110 --> 00:37:44.130
Everyone congratulated him.

00:37:44.130 --> 00:37:46.880
Lester, another
coworker, predicted

00:37:46.880 --> 00:37:49.430
that Sanjeev would be
promoted to vice president

00:37:49.430 --> 00:37:51.500
in two months, maximum.

00:37:51.500 --> 00:37:54.260
People devoured the samosas
and dutifully admired

00:37:54.260 --> 00:37:57.530
the freshly-painted ceilings
and walls, the hanging plants,

00:37:57.530 --> 00:38:01.040
the bay windows, the silk
paintings from Jaipur.

00:38:01.040 --> 00:38:04.640
But most of all they admired
Twinkle and her brocaded salwar

00:38:04.640 --> 00:38:07.520
kameez, which was the
shade of a persimmon,

00:38:07.520 --> 00:38:10.400
with a low scoop in the back,
and a little string of white

00:38:10.400 --> 00:38:13.880
rose petals she had coiled
cleverly around her head,

00:38:13.880 --> 00:38:16.640
and the pearl choker with
a sapphire at its center

00:38:16.640 --> 00:38:18.640
that adorned her throat.

00:38:18.640 --> 00:38:22.160
Over hectic jazz records played
under Twinkle's supervision,

00:38:22.160 --> 00:38:24.920
they laughed at her
anecdotes and observations,

00:38:24.920 --> 00:38:28.430
forming a widening circle around
her while Sanjeev replenished

00:38:28.430 --> 00:38:31.340
the samosas that he kept
warming in the oven,

00:38:31.340 --> 00:38:33.320
and getting ice for
people's drinks,

00:38:33.320 --> 00:38:35.240
and opening more
bottles of champagne--

00:38:35.240 --> 00:38:38.339
with some difficulty, and
explaining for the 40th time

00:38:38.339 --> 00:38:39.380
that he wasn't Christian.

00:38:39.380 --> 00:38:41.220
[LAUGHTER]

00:38:41.220 --> 00:38:43.790
It was Twinkle who led them
in separate groups up and down

00:38:43.790 --> 00:38:46.640
the winding staircase to
gaze at the back lawn,

00:38:46.640 --> 00:38:48.980
to peer down the cellar steps.

00:38:48.980 --> 00:38:51.620
"Your friends adore the
poster in my study,"

00:38:51.620 --> 00:38:53.750
she mentioned to
him triumphantly,

00:38:53.750 --> 00:38:57.620
placing her hand on the small of
his back as they, at one point,

00:38:57.620 --> 00:38:59.940
brushed past each other.

00:38:59.940 --> 00:39:01.800
Sanjeev went to
the kitchen, which

00:39:01.800 --> 00:39:04.560
was empty, and ate a piece
of chicken out of the tray

00:39:04.560 --> 00:39:06.540
on the counter with
his fingers because he

00:39:06.540 --> 00:39:08.430
thought no one was looking.

00:39:08.430 --> 00:39:10.620
He ate a second piece,
then washed it down

00:39:10.620 --> 00:39:14.190
with a gulp of gin
straight from the bottle.

00:39:14.190 --> 00:39:15.450
"Great house.

00:39:15.450 --> 00:39:16.910
Great rice."

00:39:16.910 --> 00:39:19.890
Junil, an anaesthesiologist,
walked in,

00:39:19.890 --> 00:39:22.470
spooning food from his
paper plate into his mouth.

00:39:22.470 --> 00:39:24.870
"Do you have more champagne?"

00:39:24.870 --> 00:39:28.630
"Your wife's wow," added
Prabal, following behind.

00:39:28.630 --> 00:39:31.500
He was an unmarried
professor of physics at Yale.

00:39:31.500 --> 00:39:35.430
For a moment Sanjeev stared
at him blankly, then blushed.

00:39:35.430 --> 00:39:37.440
Once at a dinner
party Prabal had

00:39:37.440 --> 00:39:41.910
pronounced that Sophia Loren
was wow, as was Audrey Hepburn.

00:39:41.910 --> 00:39:44.130
"Does she have a sister?"

00:39:44.130 --> 00:39:46.530
Junil picked a raisin
out of the rice tray.

00:39:46.530 --> 00:39:48.660
"Is her last name little star?"

00:39:48.660 --> 00:39:50.520
[LAUGHTER]

00:39:50.520 --> 00:39:54.380
The two men laughed and started
eating more rice from the tray,

00:39:54.380 --> 00:39:57.270
plowing through it with
their plastic spoons.

00:39:57.270 --> 00:40:00.270
Sanjeev went down to the
cellar for more liquor.

00:40:00.270 --> 00:40:02.820
For a few minutes he
paused on the steps

00:40:02.820 --> 00:40:05.760
in the damp, cool silence,
hugging the second crate

00:40:05.760 --> 00:40:08.460
of champagne to his chest
as the party drifted

00:40:08.460 --> 00:40:10.230
above the rafters.

00:40:10.230 --> 00:40:14.300
Then he set the reinforcements
on the dining table.

00:40:14.300 --> 00:40:15.890
"Yes, everything.

00:40:15.890 --> 00:40:19.850
We found them all in the house,
in the most unusual places,"

00:40:19.850 --> 00:40:22.140
he heard Twinkle saying
in the living room.

00:40:22.140 --> 00:40:24.170
"In fact, we keep finding them."

00:40:24.170 --> 00:40:25.220
"No!"

00:40:25.220 --> 00:40:25.970
"Yes.

00:40:25.970 --> 00:40:27.650
Every day is like
a treasure hunt.

00:40:27.650 --> 00:40:28.880
It's too good.

00:40:28.880 --> 00:40:30.770
God only knows what
else we'll find--

00:40:30.770 --> 00:40:31.910
no pun intended."

00:40:31.910 --> 00:40:33.560
[LAUGHTER]

00:40:33.560 --> 00:40:35.330
That was what started it.

00:40:35.330 --> 00:40:38.270
As if by some unspoken
pact, the whole party

00:40:38.270 --> 00:40:41.210
joined forces and began combing
through each of the rooms--

00:40:41.210 --> 00:40:42.050
[LAUGHTER]

00:40:42.050 --> 00:40:44.480
Opening closets on
their own, peering

00:40:44.480 --> 00:40:47.780
under chairs and cushions,
feeling behind curtains,

00:40:47.780 --> 00:40:49.860
removing books from bookcases.

00:40:49.860 --> 00:40:52.580
Groups scampered, giggling
and swaying, up and down

00:40:52.580 --> 00:40:54.566
the winding staircase.

00:40:54.566 --> 00:40:55.940
"We've never
explored the attic,"

00:40:55.940 --> 00:40:59.810
Twinkle announced suddenly,
and so everybody followed.

00:40:59.810 --> 00:41:01.319
"How do we get up there?"

00:41:01.319 --> 00:41:03.110
"There's a ladder in
the hallway, somewhere

00:41:03.110 --> 00:41:05.130
in the ceiling."

00:41:05.130 --> 00:41:08.120
Wearily Sanjeev followed
at the back of the crowd

00:41:08.120 --> 00:41:10.580
to point out the
location of the ladder,

00:41:10.580 --> 00:41:12.590
but Twinkle had already
found it on her own.

00:41:12.590 --> 00:41:13.130
"Eureka!"

00:41:13.130 --> 00:41:14.990
she hollered.

00:41:14.990 --> 00:41:17.570
Douglas pulled the chain
that released the steps.

00:41:17.570 --> 00:41:20.750
His face was flushed, and he
was wearing Nora's feathered hat

00:41:20.750 --> 00:41:21.290
on his head.

00:41:21.290 --> 00:41:22.610
[LAUGHTER]

00:41:22.610 --> 00:41:25.070
One by one the
guests disappeared,

00:41:25.070 --> 00:41:28.100
men helping women as they
placed their strappy high heels

00:41:28.100 --> 00:41:30.200
on the narrow slats
of the ladder,

00:41:30.200 --> 00:41:32.030
the Indian women
wrapping the free ends

00:41:32.030 --> 00:41:35.060
of their expensive saris
into their waistbands.

00:41:35.060 --> 00:41:38.420
The men followed behind,
all quickly disappearing,

00:41:38.420 --> 00:41:40.520
until Sanjeev alone
remained at the top

00:41:40.520 --> 00:41:42.440
of the winding staircase.

00:41:42.440 --> 00:41:45.210
Footsteps thundered
over his head.

00:41:45.210 --> 00:41:47.144
He had no desire to join them.

00:41:47.144 --> 00:41:48.935
He wondered if the
ceiling would collapse--

00:41:48.935 --> 00:41:49.910
[LAUGHTER]

00:41:49.910 --> 00:41:53.510
Imagined for a split second
the sight of all the tumbling

00:41:53.510 --> 00:41:57.980
drunk, perfumed bodies
crashing tangled around him.

00:41:57.980 --> 00:42:00.800
He heard a shriek, and
then rising, spreading

00:42:00.800 --> 00:42:03.500
waves of laughter
in discordant tones.

00:42:03.500 --> 00:42:04.850
Something fell.

00:42:04.850 --> 00:42:06.510
Something else shattered.

00:42:06.510 --> 00:42:08.900
He could hear them
babbling about a trunk.

00:42:08.900 --> 00:42:11.150
They seemed to be
struggling to get it open,

00:42:11.150 --> 00:42:14.560
banging feverishly
on its surface.

00:42:14.560 --> 00:42:17.470
He thought perhaps Twinkle
would call for his assistance,

00:42:17.470 --> 00:42:19.540
but he was not summoned.

00:42:19.540 --> 00:42:21.910
He looked about the
hallway and to the landing

00:42:21.910 --> 00:42:25.570
below, at the champagne
glasses and half-eaten samosas,

00:42:25.570 --> 00:42:27.190
and napkins smeared
with lipstick

00:42:27.190 --> 00:42:31.090
abandoned in every corner,
on every available surface.

00:42:31.090 --> 00:42:33.340
Then he noticed that
Twinkle in her haste

00:42:33.340 --> 00:42:35.860
had discarded her
shoes altogether,

00:42:35.860 --> 00:42:37.900
for they lay by the
foot of the ladder,

00:42:37.900 --> 00:42:40.210
black patent-leather
mules with heels

00:42:40.210 --> 00:42:43.570
like golf tees, open
toes, and slightly soiled

00:42:43.570 --> 00:42:47.920
silk labels on the instep
where her soles had rested.

00:42:47.920 --> 00:42:50.440
He placed them in the
doorway of the master bedroom

00:42:50.440 --> 00:42:54.020
so that no one would
trip when they descended.

00:42:54.020 --> 00:42:56.580
He heard something
creaking open slowly.

00:42:56.580 --> 00:43:00.980
The strident voices had
subsided to an even murmur.

00:43:00.980 --> 00:43:05.210
It occurred to Sanjeev that he
had the house all to himself.

00:43:05.210 --> 00:43:08.810
The music had ended and he
could hear, if he concentrated,

00:43:08.810 --> 00:43:11.750
the hum of the refrigerator
and the rustle of the last

00:43:11.750 --> 00:43:15.140
leaves on the trees outside and
the tapping of their branches

00:43:15.140 --> 00:43:17.210
against the window panes.

00:43:17.210 --> 00:43:19.790
With one flick of his hand
he could snap the ladder back

00:43:19.790 --> 00:43:22.340
on its spring into the
ceiling, and they would

00:43:22.340 --> 00:43:23.750
have no way of getting down--

00:43:23.750 --> 00:43:24.300
[LAUGHTER]

00:43:24.300 --> 00:43:28.250
Unless he were to pull
the chain and let them.

00:43:28.250 --> 00:43:31.520
He thought of all the things
he could do undisturbed.

00:43:31.520 --> 00:43:34.850
He could sweep Twinkle's
menagerie into a garbage bag

00:43:34.850 --> 00:43:37.310
and get in the car and
drive it to the dump,

00:43:37.310 --> 00:43:39.497
and tear down the
poster of weeping Jesus,

00:43:39.497 --> 00:43:41.830
and take a hammer to the
Virgin Mary while he was at it.

00:43:41.830 --> 00:43:43.130
[LAUGHTER]

00:43:43.130 --> 00:43:45.830
Then he would return
to the empty house.

00:43:45.830 --> 00:43:48.440
He could easily clear up the
cups and plates in an hour's

00:43:48.440 --> 00:43:51.140
time, and pour himself
a gin and tonic,

00:43:51.140 --> 00:43:54.770
and eat a plate of warmed rice,
and listen to his new box CD

00:43:54.770 --> 00:43:57.205
while reading the liner
notes, so as to understand it

00:43:57.205 --> 00:43:57.705
properly.

00:43:57.705 --> 00:43:59.240
[LAUGHTER]

00:43:59.240 --> 00:44:01.910
He nudged the ladder
slightly, but it was sturdily

00:44:01.910 --> 00:44:03.760
planted against the floor.

00:44:03.760 --> 00:44:06.770
Bodging it would
require some effort.

00:44:06.770 --> 00:44:11.630
"My god, I need a cigarette,"
Twinkle exclaimed from above.

00:44:11.630 --> 00:44:14.600
Sanjeev felt knots forming
at the back of his neck.

00:44:14.600 --> 00:44:15.830
He felt dizzy.

00:44:15.830 --> 00:44:17.570
He needed to lie down.

00:44:17.570 --> 00:44:20.180
He walked toward the
bedroom, but stopped short

00:44:20.180 --> 00:44:23.930
when he saw Twinkle's shoes
facing him in the doorway.

00:44:23.930 --> 00:44:26.610
He thought of her
slipping them on her feet.

00:44:26.610 --> 00:44:28.520
But instead of
feeling irritated,

00:44:28.520 --> 00:44:32.000
as he had ever since they'd
moved into the house together,

00:44:32.000 --> 00:44:34.670
he felt a pang of
anticipation at the thought

00:44:34.670 --> 00:44:38.210
of her rushing unsteadily down
the winding staircase in them,

00:44:38.210 --> 00:44:41.000
scratching the floor
a bit in her path.

00:44:41.000 --> 00:44:42.680
The pang intensified
as he thought

00:44:42.680 --> 00:44:45.920
of her rushing to the bathroom
to brighten her lipstick,

00:44:45.920 --> 00:44:48.470
and eventually rushing to
get people their coats,

00:44:48.470 --> 00:44:50.990
and finally rushing to
the cherrywood table

00:44:50.990 --> 00:44:53.450
when the last guest had
left, to begin opening

00:44:53.450 --> 00:44:55.750
their housewarming presents.

00:44:55.750 --> 00:44:58.962
It was the same pang he used to
feel before they were married,

00:44:58.962 --> 00:45:00.670
when he would hang up
the phone after one

00:45:00.670 --> 00:45:03.220
of their conversations, or
when he would drive back

00:45:03.220 --> 00:45:06.100
from the airport, wondering
which ascending plane

00:45:06.100 --> 00:45:08.140
in the sky was hers.

00:45:08.140 --> 00:45:10.600
"Sanj, you won't believe this."

00:45:10.600 --> 00:45:14.020
She emerged with her back to
him, her hands over her head,

00:45:14.020 --> 00:45:16.780
the tops of her bare
shoulder blades perspiring,

00:45:16.780 --> 00:45:19.750
supporting something
still hidden from view.

00:45:19.750 --> 00:45:20.710
"You got it, Twinkle?"

00:45:20.710 --> 00:45:21.790
someone asked.

00:45:21.790 --> 00:45:23.650
"Yes, you can let go."

00:45:23.650 --> 00:45:26.920
Now he saw that her hands
were wrapped around it--

00:45:26.920 --> 00:45:30.970
a solid silver bust of Christ,
the head easily three times

00:45:30.970 --> 00:45:31.960
the size of his own.

00:45:31.960 --> 00:45:33.250
[LAUGHTER]

00:45:33.250 --> 00:45:35.650
It had a patrician
bump on its nose,

00:45:35.650 --> 00:45:39.010
magnificent curly hair that
rested atop a pronounced collar

00:45:39.010 --> 00:45:42.190
bone, and a broad
forehead that reflected

00:45:42.190 --> 00:45:46.240
in miniature the walls and doors
and lampshades around them.

00:45:46.240 --> 00:45:50.740
Its expression was confident,
as if assured of its devotees,

00:45:50.740 --> 00:45:53.770
the unyielding lips
sensuous and full.

00:45:53.770 --> 00:45:56.020
It was also sporting
Nora's feathered hat.

00:45:56.020 --> 00:45:57.030
[LAUGHTER]

00:45:57.030 --> 00:45:59.860
As Twinkle descended,
Sanjeev put his hands

00:45:59.860 --> 00:46:01.990
around her waist to balance her.

00:46:01.990 --> 00:46:03.550
And he relieved her
of the bust when

00:46:03.550 --> 00:46:05.320
she had reached the ground.

00:46:05.320 --> 00:46:08.140
It weighed a good 30 pounds.

00:46:08.140 --> 00:46:10.810
The others began lowering
themselves slowly,

00:46:10.810 --> 00:46:12.640
exhausted from the hunt.

00:46:12.640 --> 00:46:16.560
Some trickled downstairs
in search of a fresh drink.

00:46:16.560 --> 00:46:20.645
She took a breath, raised her
eyebrows, crossed her fingers.

00:46:20.645 --> 00:46:23.145
"Would you mind terribly if we
displayed it on the mantle--"

00:46:23.145 --> 00:46:24.270
[LAUGHTER]

00:46:24.270 --> 00:46:25.650
"Just for tonight.

00:46:25.650 --> 00:46:27.540
I know you hate it."

00:46:27.540 --> 00:46:28.860
He did hate it.

00:46:28.860 --> 00:46:32.940
He hated its immensity, and
its flawless, polished surface,

00:46:32.940 --> 00:46:35.340
and its undeniable value.

00:46:35.340 --> 00:46:38.970
He hated that it was in his
house and that he owned it.

00:46:38.970 --> 00:46:40.950
Unlike the other
things they had found,

00:46:40.950 --> 00:46:45.270
this contained dignity,
solemnity, beauty even.

00:46:45.270 --> 00:46:47.040
But to his surprise,
these qualities

00:46:47.040 --> 00:46:48.930
made him hate it all the more.

00:46:48.930 --> 00:46:53.270
Most of all, he hated it because
he knew that Twinkle loved it.

00:46:53.270 --> 00:46:56.030
"I'll keep it in my study
from tomorrow," Twinkle added.

00:46:56.030 --> 00:46:57.800
"I promise."

00:46:57.800 --> 00:47:00.680
She would never put it
in her study, he knew.

00:47:00.680 --> 00:47:02.150
For the rest of
their days together

00:47:02.150 --> 00:47:04.850
she would keep it on the
center of the mantle, flanked

00:47:04.850 --> 00:47:07.820
on either side by the
rest of the menagerie.

00:47:07.820 --> 00:47:09.560
Each time they had
guests Twinkle would

00:47:09.560 --> 00:47:11.420
explain how she had found it.

00:47:11.420 --> 00:47:14.270
And they would admire
her as they listened.

00:47:14.270 --> 00:47:17.090
He gazed at the crushed
rose petals in her hair,

00:47:17.090 --> 00:47:19.740
at the pearl and sapphire
choker at her throat,

00:47:19.740 --> 00:47:23.090
at the sparkly crimson
polish on her toes.

00:47:23.090 --> 00:47:25.310
He decided that these
were among the things that

00:47:25.310 --> 00:47:28.580
made Prabal think she was wow.

00:47:28.580 --> 00:47:31.130
His head ached from
gin and his arms ached

00:47:31.130 --> 00:47:32.810
from the weight of the statue.

00:47:32.810 --> 00:47:36.080
He said, "I put your
shoes in the bedroom."

00:47:36.080 --> 00:47:38.300
"Thanks, but my feet
are killing me."

00:47:38.300 --> 00:47:40.490
Twinkle gave his
elbow a little squeeze

00:47:40.490 --> 00:47:42.500
and headed for the living room.

00:47:42.500 --> 00:47:44.570
Sanjeev pressed the
massive silver face

00:47:44.570 --> 00:47:48.320
to his ribs, careful not to
let the feathered hat slip,

00:47:48.320 --> 00:47:50.790
and followed her.

00:47:50.790 --> 00:47:51.630
Thank you.

00:47:51.630 --> 00:47:54.980
[APPLAUSE]

